//// @hidden
//// Independent CBOR vectors checked with Lucid Evolution 0.6.2's CML.
//// Script-data hashes are calculated by CML.hash_script_data; transaction bodies
//// are decoded and round-tripped with CML without Aiken reconstruction helpers.
//// CML rejects the missing_outputs negative vector for omitting mandatory key 1.
//// The cost model is Scalus 1.3.0's bundled Preview Plutus V3 model.
//// The ordinary input is 10..10#0, collateral is 90..90#0, and optional
//// reference input is a0..a0#0. Withdrawal uses script 02..02 at pointer (3, 0).
//// Its budget is 17,500,000 memory and 10,000,000,000 CPU. Fee is 1,000,000,
//// total collateral 1,500,000, and returned collateral 98,500,000 lovelace.
//// configured_cpu uses 9,500,000,000 CPU; configured_memory uses 17,000,000
//// memory. Each preserves the other budget and uses builtin_false arguments.
//// Ordinary outputs use the canonical empty array, except negative vectors
//// named with_one_output, with_multiple_outputs, successful_matching_return_output,
//// missing_outputs, indefinite_empty_outputs, and nonminimal_empty_outputs.
//// Network is zero except constants ending in _mainnet.
//// Valid direct-mode vectors hash `DirectArguments` constructor 0. The
//// `reference_arguments*` vectors hash `ReferenceArguments` constructor 1 and
//// commit the failed transaction's three ordered reference inputs.

